#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_adventure_erotic/0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Together they joined forces to rule the galaxy."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_adventure_erotic/0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Xander inseminated him <i>real</i> good."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "BANG! A shrieking gunshot pierced the silence, and a gasping Hunky McCoy collapsed: dead."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Shocked, a panicked Xander swiveled around to find Luscious — blood splattered across her face and the revolver still clenched in her trembling hands..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "\"You don't understand,\" Luscious whispered breathlessly, \"My step-brother had to die. If I hadn't stopped him, he was planning to...\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "\"Murder you, Xander, and take the ranch for himself!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "\"Become a wedding planner who never got married himself!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "\"Become a superhero!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0/27/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Have passionate, carnal sex with us... <i>forever.</i>\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Apparently the Lusty Lasso Ranch had historical significance or something — which was a huge tourism draw specifically for German nuns and absolutely no one else."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And as the nuns descended from their cut-rate tour bus — and were immediately greeted by the moaning, writhing pile of passion — they instantly..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Burned the barn to ashes & swore each other to secrecy."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Caught the wind in their cornettes and sailed away."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Proceeded to steal various national monuments."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Disrobed (both figuratively & actually) to join in."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "For unbeknownst to the trio, the Lusty Lasso Ranch had been built upon the remains of a secret, ancient Freemason temple: a temple that contained <i>billions</i> of dollars in gold and priceless relics."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And as the trio writhed in ecstasy, hundreds of feet below them, adventurer Julian Montpelier had finally secured the prize he'd spent his whole life searching for..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Irrefutable proof he didn't murder his wife."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "A mask that transformed him into his cartoon-esque alter ego."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "A dead president's bejeweled funerary skull."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_adventure/0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "The world's most perfect dildo."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What had begun as a run-of-the-mill, country tryst, had quickly escalated into a breathless, pulse-pounding orgy."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And as wave after wave of pleasure rushed through Xander's quivering loins, he realized there was only one thing that would make this moment <i>even</i> better..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "A new mystery to solve. So he created one."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "If everyone had flatulence. So they did."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/18/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "A nuclear apocalypse — which coincidentally had just begun."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/erotic_erotic_erotic_erotic/0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "If everyone in the entire world joined. So they did."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a twist - what a commentary on the American cannery industry! Pure noir - I call it \"The Ink was Black as Night.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So Santa was a hitman for Pazzoli and killed Cliff? Huh. I call it \"Yule Be Sorry.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Okay - this seemed very noir up until the end. But at that point readers will be hooked!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I call it \"Night of the Assassins.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Daphne appears in the threshold - and says \"...care to join\"?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_noir_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I like it - a slow burn romance. I call it \"Mystery of the Missing Kiss.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Avenging Cliff's mysterious disappearance... probably! Redefining the genre. I call it \"Best Served Cold.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "He can pay off his office rent now! Okay... I call it \"Detective Chef: Death and Dessert.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Saving Sprawlsville... I guess? I call it \"Birthday Blowout.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Gregor and Wen make love covered in cream. Hm. I call it \"Communist Man-Undressed-O.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Damn, just how justice is served in Sprawlsville. Let's call this grim tale 'Cannoli's Are Best Served Gold'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Problem solved! All the best stories end there. Let's call it 'From Fatale to Florida'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This case brought by Daphne ended up being way bigger than we thought! Let's call this 'Cliff's Notes: Book One'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "You mean... finding yourself attracted to inanimate objects? I don't think this will sell well at all. Let's call it 'Crate Everything'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Detective Wen decides not to tell Daphne, as there's nothing more shameful than being a Dough Boy. Let's call this 'Cream Filling'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The joke was on Xander all along then! Although he did get some cannolis out of the deal. Let's call this 'Dough or Dough Not'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's a tricky fight, but in the end Xander wins and finds Cliff, huddled in a corner, forced to wear the Dough Boys' tight fitted t-shirt. Let's call it 'The Case of the Hasty Pastry'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "There was no one more loving than big Jersey. His tendency to surround himself with goons was only because he had too much love to keep to just himself."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_noir_erotic_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one \"Who's Cliff?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Just another cold day in Winnipeg. Let's call this one 'Canadian Standoff'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff turns out to be fantastic at finding great snacks, and Gregor's stories help ease the boredom on the long road to Anchorage. Let's call it - 'Car We There Yet?'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "At last, the streets lay glittering before them. All feuds were settled, thanks to Gregor's father serving as their treasure map. I call it - 'Urning a Living'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The fearsome foursome flung themselves upon each other with reckless abandon. Upon returning to Sprawlsville the following week, Gregor realized they forgot where they left the urn."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_noir_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one - 'Dude, Where's My Urn?'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Mastermind behind what? This one doesn't seem to add up, though I guess books don't always have to. Let's call it - 'Not So Fast'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The kids are all orphans, and Gregor and Xander take them under their wings to take them to the Olympics. Let's call it 'The Mighty Canucks'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Good for him! I guess we can just write whatever we want and it comes true, huh? Let's call this 'World's Fastest Detective'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yep, Wanda sure was good looking, and she earned top marks in bed. Let's call this tale 'Where's Wanda?'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "With Detective Wen's penchant for espionage, the pair sneak their way through Canada's finest, and score a victory for Poland at long last. Let's call this 'Krakow Calling'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The burger was excellent, toasty and firm."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hey, maybe this is a cookbook! Let's call it '101 Best Recipes for Smuggling'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The fight atop the pylon was one for the history books - Gregor fell to his death, just like his father before him. Let's call it - 'Border Crossings'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "As the border patrol guards close in on them, Gregor and Xander share a kiss that had been boiling inside them for so long. It's the last thing they do as the shots go off..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_adventure_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Wow! Let's call this one - 'Forbidden Crimes - A Communist Manifesto'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Incredible - I never saw it coming that it had the twist of a noir right up until the end. I call it \"Deadly Detours.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Amazing - they were twins the whole time. Even though we never foreshadowed it - comedy gold! I call it \"Never the Twins Shall Meet.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hm... Seems very left field that 'aliens came in'? I'll call it 'Red Planet: Revolution'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_comedy_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander responds 'Oh I can bring the heat.' Now this - starting with a fake femme fatale and ending with an erotic road trip? I call it \"The Highway Was Paved with Kisses and Flesh.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah of course! This is the kind of book that I'll leave a video essayist to explain to our audience later. I call it 'Lest the Pirate Becomes You.'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh right! I'll be sure to put lots of jokes in there somewhere, especially for the squid cannery part. I'll call it 'Squid Squirts' and put a big smiley face on the cover."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'll make sure the battle is the majority of the book then. I'll call it 'Detective vs. Communist vs. Pirates'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "In one fell swoop we've fixed the problems! Kisses for all - especially the pirates. I'll call it 'Pirate Investigations'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh dear, reflecting on our own 'bread and circuses' model for society. The Mayor and Shrug working together to distract from the decaying underbelly, with pirates to entertain the masses. I call it - 'City Sails'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander and Gregor are so hilariously bad that Shrug can't help but reveal that Cliff was inside the captain's hold all along playing mahjong! It's called 'Worst Verse'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "To battle! Xander's training as a fencer allows him to thrust his way through all the dancers and defeat Shrug, who was holding Cliff captive as cargo!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I call it 'Forbidden Goods'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The tension was still too much between Gregor and Xander, and everyone knows communists and detectives can't kiss."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_comedy_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This will be the first in the slow burn romance series called 'Fatale Whispers'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Tragic... suicide by pirate to save her husband, who was being held hostage. I call it 'Slash and Burn'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well then that solves everything for Xander, who can now buy all the candy he ever wanted without any adult to say no. I call it 'Dreams Do Come True'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Gregor's past as a bomb defuser is only outmatched by Xander's capability for doing cool flips off the sides of pirate ships."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The spectacular end will make a great movie. I call it 'Big Time Boat Blasts'!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "No one can resist the taut muscles and lithe dexterity of the barbarians."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "While the orgy takes place on the poop deck, Xander slips away and finds Cliff among the gyrating bodies, smiling radiantly."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_adventure_erotic/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I call it - 'Oil and Water'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The closer we zoom in on the fractal of Sprawlsville... the weirder it gets. Let's call this heady trip 'Inside Doubt'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It is. It is so funny to think about pirates kissing. Haha. Let's call this one 'Pirates: Kissing!'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The ancient golden squid was right under Xander's nose the whole time! Gregor saves the day I imagine. I call it 'Fool's Gold'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_adventure_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Pirates for so long have been maligned as poor lovers. This book aims to fix that. I call it 'Ahoy, Mating'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A choice between being with the ones you love and protecting them from mobsters. I call this tragic tale 'Rambling Debts'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Bureaucracies do be like that - one spelling mistake can lead your whole life astray! Fortunately, Xander fixes the typo and all is well. I call it - 'Lotto Correct'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff and Xander work on an escape plan over the course of several months to bring him back home. I call it - 'Canary in the Cannery'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hmm, I'll see what I can do. This might be for a very specific reader with very specific interests... but at least they'll be satisfied. I call it 'Torque'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "You're right, we can skip the writing part and just do a summary! It'll be 12 pages and be called 'One Detective Story Is Inside This Book'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The origin story of Wen-Wen the Clown! I can see this becoming a series for children who love clowns! I call it 'Remember Wen-Wen'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Of course - we'll fill in the details later about what the fuck those are. Let's call it '12 Grails: The Embarkation'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sure, we can set up more amazingly written coincidences just like that one. Let's call it 'Who Has a Mystery for Me, Please?'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Those damn titans of industry - they know a detective's greatest weakness! Let's call this one 'Irresistible Clues'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a funny twist! Then we can sell Detective Wen plushies! Let's call it 'Fritto Mister'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It'll be up to Xander to take down the canning industry to avenge Cliff and bring him back to Daphne. If he can fend off Gregor's goons... Let's call it 'I Think. I Can.'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The origin story of Detective Wen's strapping partner Bobbie Brawn! I call it 'Searching for Bobbie Fisher'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yes yes, of course. We were writing a mystery, weren't we? Let's call this 'Pay No Attention to Chapter 5'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Funny stuff! It can be an abstract ending - no one would be expecting that, not even us authors! Let's call it 'The Power of the Pelvis'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a twist... the goons are outmatched by Xander's gymnastics and Cliff is saved! Let's call it 'Cliff Jumping'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_noir_erotic_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Uh huh, okay. Yep. Those will all be featured. Let's just title it that."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A tragic end - as everyone in Sprawlsville was a clone the whole time. Seems like it's better to not stick your nose where it doesn't belong. Let's call this 'Detectives All the Way Down'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The Mayor's plan never would have worked since Cliff is a free-thinker, well-educated, and a decent dude. Sprawlsville thrives with good citizenry and clean-smelling clothes."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_noir_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this 'Infinite Cliffs'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A thrilling conclusion! At the end the Mayor's manor even explodes! Let's call this 'Ballot Busted'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "They make love as Cliff watches. Xander feels like a real Detective now, and Felicia, a Queen. Let's call this 'Bestowing the Title'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The reality show empire had gone too far - but the viewers don't lie. No matter Xander's exposés, reality tv was here to stay. Let's call this 'Not Suitable for Viewing'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander never needed to be a detective anyway, and happily accepted the title 'Chef'. Let's call this 'As Scene on TV'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Victor Pudi Vana never expected the gunshot, and the ratings were never higher. Let's call this one 'Series Finale'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff moaned huskily, and Princess Felicia (a porn actress by trade) gave her best performance for the cameras. Let's call this one 'A Very Special Episode'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Succumbing to the shinobi poison, Princess Felicia died in Xander's arms."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_noir/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But with his new title, he rescues Cliff and brings him to Daphne - who is forever grateful. Let's call this 'Sunrise Surprise'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander pays the requisite amount. The book immediately ends. Let's call this 'For a Price'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Fighting their way through the Mayor's laser attacks and the dreaded Reverse Ninjas, Xander, Felicia, and Cliff make it out in one piece as the Mayor's manor explodes behind them."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this 'Requiem for a Team'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander gave his Princess her reward while Cliff looked on horrified. Eventually I suppose he was rescued and the case solved. Let's call this 'Silent Night'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Putting aside his erotic feelings, Xander truly earned the title of Detective that day. Turned out that Daphne sold her husband to the Mayor for votes! Let's call this 'Birth of a Gumshoe'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Princess Felicia says yes, more because she thinks he asks her to \"carry\" him."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Across the threshold of the Mayor's house, and into their fine new lodgings underneath the awnings of the Thai restaurant on 5th."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_comedy/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The smells of Pad See Ew each night are as intoxicating as their love for each other. Let's call this 'Glossed and Found'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The shootout was fierce, but Xander, Felicia, and Cliff made it out alive. Cliff revealed that he was planning to run against the Mayor - and now he had the freedom and breath to actually win!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander earns his detective's license and gets the title! Let's call this one 'Electoral Spottage'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It was too good to pass up. Ball-gag in mouth and a nice whipping from Princess Felicia and Cliff, Xander lived in the Mayor's basement for the rest of his days."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_noir_erotic_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'll call it 'A Place for Everything'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Clear as day - there was Cliff, kept prisoner by his own wife to extort detectives around the city! The case was solved. Let's call it 'Enter the 13th Chamber'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Blasting off into outer space, Xander landed on Planet Detective, where only Detectives lived."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sadly he was denied entry as he wasn't one."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_comedy/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one - 'Escape to Planet Detective'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Greeting him at the top level was Cliff, machine gun in one hand, detonator in the other. Xander was able to disarm the gun but couldn't stop the bomb in time."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "As he fell to the ground Xander grabbed a nearby parachute. He landed right on top of the missing jewels that Cliff had stolen from the Ancient Mystery Museum."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_adventure/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one - 'Family Jewels'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The scene that greeted Xander was beyond his wildest dreams - he walks into the light and we fade to black. Let's call it - 'Star 69'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's always insurance fraud, always. Let's call this tragic tale 'King Fear'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The kingdom of candy was a delight for everyone in Sprawlsville, although there were no social safety nets. Let's call this 'The Sweet Life'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The war was bloody and relentless. Thousands died, though it was worth the cost. Xander won the fabled Prom Grail. Let's call this 'The Blood Oozes at Midnight'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "They were forever enshrined in Sprawlsville High legend, though not as famous as the captain of the football team who became the Mayor. Let's call this 'Court Is Now in Session'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The poisoner herself. She laughed as she revealed that this was a ruse to remove Sprawlsville from pretend detectives. Let's call this cautionary tale - 'Be Careful What You Fish For'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "F. Murray Abragham had saved countless reunions from poison using his forbidden concoction. Xander drank it and decided that janitors are ultimately more helpful than detectives."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this strange tale - 'Clean Sweep'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The gunslinger's moustache fell off to reveal Cliff Fatale! He was there to murder Daphne for revenge on not letting him win Prom King 20 years ago!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "After the smoke from the shootout settled, there was one left standing. Newly minted detective Xander Wen."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_adventure/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one - 'Reunions Are for Suckers'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Using a variety of trade kisses and cuddles, the poison left Xander's body. In return, Xander became a streetwalker just like Felicia. Let's call this - 'Birth of a Geisha'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "When first starting in any industry, it's difficult. Let's call this - 'Tears of a Defective Detective'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "He brought back to the office: 46 dumplings, 2 oranges, half a cake, 4 bags of chips, and a ladle. Score."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_erotic_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This will be called 'The Big Heist'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It was a thrilling conclusion to a very weird tale. Xander wasn't a detective, but he did become a viral sensation. Let's call this 'Swing, Swing, Swing!'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_comedy_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It worked like a charm, and Daphne and Xander soon married. The husband was never found, but Xander did inherit a sweet big house. Let's call this 'Operation Infiltration'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "With such a display of competence and restraint, Xander gets his Detective license, and maybe we tease a romance with Daphne... I call it 'Twisted Flames, Twisted Heartbreak'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Everything dissolves, including Cliff who was made mostly out of drugs! The Vantablack Market quickly closes down, and the children of Sprawlsville are safe from crime."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_noir_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander gains a Detective license, and we are set up for another book! Let's call this - 'Like Water Off a Drug's Back'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's violence, and lots of it! After the bullets fly, only Xander is left standing, with a whole lotta drugs to sell. Let's call this - 'Vantage Point'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff turned to drug-peddling only because his marriage to Daphne was lacking. The turbulent affair with Xander is the stuff of legends. Let's call this - 'Cliff Diving'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Daphne pays Xander a cool five hundo, and Xander becomes a real Detective. I'll call it - 'Doing the Job of Detective'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "As a twosome, Xander and Cliff were to be feared. They won all the biggest tourneys, and got the best gaming chairs as prizes."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_comedy_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call this one - 'Climbing Down the Ranks'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The nerds were easily stopped by a detective's best weapon - gun. Xander brought coolness back to the underworld, and the nerds never came back. Let's call this - 'No Nerds, No Words'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff nodded slowly, and two days later they were married. They are currently working on a full 10'x10' diorama of their favorite ogre battle. Let's call this - 'Underworld Overture'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff offers a higher sum for Xander's silence. Because in the city of Sprawlsville, detectives are bought and sold like so many green beans. Let's call this - 'The Curtain Falls'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff looks down to see that Xander has tricked him. His goons laugh, and a smile even creeps on Cliff's face, too. Xander becomes a stand-up comic."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I call this one - 'The Last Laugh'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff, terrified, runs for the way out of the sewers. A bold chase ensues, ending up at the waterfall outside Daphne's house. One or both of them fall to their death."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I call this - 'From the Bottom to the Top'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "'Well all right then,' Cliff agrees. They have a great couple of nights together, but eventually part. Let's call this one - 'Carnal Carnival'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Daphne is surprised, but grateful to know her husband is okay, albeit shamefully distant. Xander receives a Detective's license and a significant pay raise. Let's call this - 'Promotional Consideration'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander's line of sex toys is the perfect foil to Cliff's. Whereas Cliff smiles, Xander scowls. It's enough to entice people to buy the product to make Xander happy."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_erotic_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A story of entrepreneurship rather than a procedural... Let's call this one '8 Secrets of Sales - A Story of Fear and Desire'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "He defeats the man in single combat. Hooray for violence! Let's call this - 'Brutal Bottoms'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_adventure_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander has a great night to himself and learns some interesting new techniques. Let's call this 'Journey to Self-Discovery - Part One'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The day is saved, and Xander frees Cliff from servitude. Even Conrad calls him 'Detective Wen' as he walks into the shower. Let's call this 'No Qualms at the Palms'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "With madcap flare, Xander sneaks the real Cliff out before Conrad can notice. He can hear the shaking fist in the distance. Let's call this 'Stakeout Sneakout.'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The swords clang and clash - and in the end Xander throws Conrad off the dock, cleansing him of the smell. Cliff is freed - and a real Detective is crowned. Let's call this 'Dueling Duellos'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, okay. I can describe that a little bit. Maybe this book is just a little short. It's called 'Squeaky Clean Getaway'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Tomato the Melon was caught at last, and the mystery solved. Let's call this - 'To Catch With Briefs'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "How embarrassing and very very funny. Let's call this laugh riot 'Whoopsies, My Butt Is Showing!'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'll summarize all that on the last page. Let's call it - 'The Hero's Journey'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Good for Xander, becoming an inspiration. I also don't wear pants. Let's call this - 'Leader Hosen'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah yes, the plot. Xander does it all and everything ends great. Let's call this 'Distracted Detective Days'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The name change took six to eight weeks, but he did save the good people of the Dismal Palms. Let's call this - 'A Stitch in Time'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Unfortunately Daphne has no reason to show up to her own... bomb? Look, even I can't make that one work. Let's end it with him becoming a tennis player. I'll call it - 'Tennis Elbows'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Kaboom! Their love was dynamite."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_adventure_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's call it 'Their Love Was Dynamite'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which we can leave the reader to decide! Glad we focused on all that lovemaking. Let's call this 'You Figure It Out'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sometimes things just work themselves out, and Xander eventually went to detective school. Let's call this 'Sleepin' Around'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Even changing the life of one person is worth it. Let's call this - 'From Violence to Science.'"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_comedy_erotic_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Okay, I think I can finish this one off myself then. Let's call this - 'Slut Stuff'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Straightforward noir! We tried to reach new heights with that Mt. Everest misdirect, but all good mysteries end at a wharf. Let's call this one \"Smugglers Fun.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, bringing in a talk show host at the very end certainly is a <i>choice</i>, but I wouldn't think mystery readers would like that. Let's warn them with the title \"The Case of the Missed Opportunity.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh. Doomzilla comes in, huh? Maybe we can foreshadow that a little in the title: \"Crushed by a Mystery.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So in the end, Xander loses Cliff but regains a former lover? I imagine they have sex."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_noir_erotic/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yeah, let's write that part too. Gotta have sex. And we'll call it \"Tangled Up in Mystery.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Just goes to show you why detectives shouldn't play guitar. Let's call it: \"Enzo Jr's Special Day.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And that ends the book as unfortunately I'm out of paper. And patience. Let's call this monstrosity: \"I Left My Silly String in San Francisco.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I always wondered where Moses left that thing. I'll say originally I wasn't sure about the tonal shifts, but I am a little tone deaf! Let's call it: \"Xander Wen and the Birthday of Doom.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And of course at the strip club is... Jeff. Or Cliff. I forget who he was looking for already. Let's call this: \"Two Guys, a Girl, and a Strip Club.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "'Forget it Xander, it's Cyborgtown,' Enzo says as they lock Xander up for good. Let's call this: \"The Cyborgian Candidate.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Aw how cute! Readers love cuteness over plot. And characters. And everything else! Let's cut to the chase and call this: \"Under the Feline Sun.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which could only mean... Cliff was a cyborg too! Xander gets a medal or something. Anyway, let's call this: \"Don't Tell Mom the President is a Cyborg.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And so begins the second book in our ten-book series where Xander uses the executive branch to find Cliff who has been hiding in the Supreme Court the whole time. Let's title it: \"The Oval Orifice.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Subverting the expectation of a 'femme fatale' and putting in a 'phlegm fatale' (because Enzo coughs a lot)! Readers won't know what to expect in: \"The Uncoughables.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And then they find the fortune teller who turns out to be Cliff all along! Right? Right. Um okay let's call this tour-de-farce \"My Tryst With the Mob Boss.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I wouldn't exactly call that a twist, but I would call it a bad idea. Still, let's title it: \"Jur-Ass-sic Lark.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_noir_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And then Xander goes \"Nyah! Nyah! Nyah!\" And then the readers go \"What! The! Hell!\" Still... there's a market for surprise erotica, right? Let's call this: \"Gulp Fiction.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a twist! Who cares about Daphne and Cliff - we need more stories about murderous talking dogs. Let's call it: \"Muncher the Talking Murder Pooch.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Huh. What a profound contemplation on the importance of a healthy diet. Let's call it: \"The Case of the Missing Husband: 20 Tips to Live a Low Carb Lifestyle.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Honestly, I don't believe in the devil, and furthermore I also don't believe in this being a good book. But maybe readers will feel differently about: \"Muncher and Xander's Unsolvable Mystery.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Honestly death by sex seems like a pretty good way to go. And even though we lost the thread, we can still title the book \"Too Much of a Good Thing: A Sexsational Mystery: Muncher the Talking Dog.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And in our case - the 'btw' stands for 'Buy This Work!' Let's call this loony lampoon: \"The Canine's Confession.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, if I see the word 'forever' it means the book is over. Let's call this caper with the sudden ending: \"It's All Good, My Best Friend Is Muncher Now.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well that ending came outta left field. But we can say that's where the hurricane started! So we should title it: \"Left Field: Where Things Aren't Right.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah. Okay. Let's call this surprise erotica: \"Detective Xander and the Case of the Subject Matter We're Not Touching with a 10ft Pole.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander found the one thing aliens were susceptible too: due process! Let's call this: \"The Day the Aliens Stood Still in Court.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which, in the end, was where both Xander and the plot of this travesty died. Let's call this \"What Happens in Vegas?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This book has it all! Dogs, nuclear weapons, aliens, and somewhere I think there was mention of a mystery? Readers won't remember once they read: \"Independence Spay.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Now I'm finally interested! Let's call this intense erotic probe into the aliens: \"The XXX-Files.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sometimes life takes us down strange horny paths... let's call this erotic-ghost-detective-tale: \"Strange Horny Paths.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which was true: a dude banging a ghost would go super viral. Let's have it end with Xander and Muncher going viral! We'll title this: \"Paranormal Sextivity.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Strong choice. Let's make an even stronger choice and end the book right there. We can call it: \"Whatever Happened to Daphne Fatale?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_comedy_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I love a happy ending. I also love a horny ending! We'll title this 'tale of woah': \"The Fornicating Phantom.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "<i>Good.</i> I'm so glad Xander arrested Larry for his moral degeneracy."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_noir/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "After all, if characters don't behave righteously, we have no choice but to assume that the author condones immoral behavior."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_noir/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's title this: \"Xander Wen and the Death of Media Literacy.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A bold and powerful statement about the masculine urge to teach a dog to play basketball. Let's call it: \"Xander Wen and the Mayor He DIDN'T Murder.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yeah volcano boarding!!! That sounds way more fun than anything else, including writing this! Let's title our righteous masterpiece: \"Assassination Averted!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "We'll say that having sex with Larry <i>was</i> Xander's personal Mt. Everest. It's a happy ending for Xander, so let's call this: \"The Sex Lives of Billionaires.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Love it! Sometimes the best projects just throw in the towel halfway through: it's called being \"avant-garde.\" Let's call this one: \"Larry Learns to Dance.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh Xander, you gotta shower! All the best detective stories have massive showering scenes — but in the end I think readers will appreciate: \"Mystery of the Two Left Feet.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "All the best books end with an unmotivated lunar colony emergency; that's indisputable. So I'm sure the public is going to go crazy for: \"Dancing on the Moon.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'm digging it! It's got a \"so unsexy it's actually sexy\" quality. Let's call it: \"When a Detective Loves a Billionaire.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sometimes a story just has to go full circle! Let's call it: \"Xander Wen Throws in the Towel.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander plays the tambourine and sings back-up. Maybe we can sell the album as a tie-in? But let's call the book part of this travesty: \"Larry Aruba's Death Wish.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And at the top of Mt. Everest? Cliff! Whether it's a real cliff or Cliff Fatale we'll let the readers decide. There's no way they won't love: \"Splat Goes the Billionaire!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Very clever. Let's call it: \"Ramblings of an Idiot.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Because Cliff killed Xander's wife, who was Daphne! And Larry was also Xander! And Cliff was also Mt. Everest! Let's call this: \"How to Host an Orgy in 10 Easy Steps.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Uh oh - Xander's parents always <i>hated</i> detectives. Critics won't like \"Who Invited My Parents to the Orgy?\" but then again readers probably won't either."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's a morality story in the end - with Xander as the Prophet and Larry Aruba as God Incarnate. Let's call this: \"Xander Wen and the Tangential Orgy.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_adventure_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And Larry is <i>really</i> big down there. Xander uses his detective skills to find out how to marry him. It's a romance! Anyway, it's call it: \"Xander Wen Gets Lucky.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I mean I'd confess to murder if you shocked me with a car battery. But, I think \"In Cold Tub\" is going to be a huge hit with anyone who wants to talk to objects!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, I did say 'to Xander's surprise.' I just didn't figure it would be <i>that</i> surprising. Anyway, let's call this: \"No Country for Old Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which all came true - making the disappearance of Cliff Fatale completely moot. Well, let's title moot-sterpiece: \"Lubestradamus.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hey, I'm not gonna say that sort of thing is impossible. Let's call this: \"Seduced by the Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a smorgasbord! You can really feel the myriad of disparate, conflicting influences. Let's call it: \"That Slippery Detective!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And who was the top competitor? None other than Cliff Fatale. Perfect. Let's call this hot pile of garbage: \"Slip Sliding Away... in Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh, a sudden turn to the occult! Everyone knows what that means - we'll fix the plot holes in the sequel! Let's call this: \"The Slippery Mystery.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Fortunately the <i>very next</i> person he saw was Cliff Fatale who was visiting a nearby deli. They had sex, too! Let's call this book-thing: \"After Everest, Everyone Needs a Sandwich.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Awesome! The use of lube in winter sports is <i>greatly</i> underappreciated. Our sports biopic will be called: \"The Talented Mr. Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander slides down Everest and into the hearts of millions. Cliff Fatale is soon found out to be Daphne herself, solving the mystery. Our book will have to be called: \"The Lube That Saved the Day!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh wow - think of the complications! Please. I don't want to think too hard. Let's title this head-scratcher: \"The Sixth Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And of course, both Cliff <i>and</i> Daphne were there! They were just getting Xander to overcome his fear of heights! Let's call it: \"Lube Me Up, Scotty.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, we can find out in <i>another</i> book that someone else can write! Let's call this one: \"Whatever Happened to Cliff Fatale?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The answer, as it happened, was eight. Which wasn't impressive, but frankly neither is: \"Call Me By Your Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Uh yeah! Then there's an earthquake. Xander's okay but his life will... never be the same? I'm not sure about this one, but maybe readers will feel differently about: \"A Lust for Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_adventure_erotic_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "In the world of our creation, it sure is! They get married and Xander takes on the lube's last name, which was Garfein. Let's title this love story: \"Fifty Shades of Lube.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Case closed! Daphne and Cliff get together and the sirens serve 10-15 years apiece. Let's call it: \"Stuck On Skyros Island with the Murdering Sirens Again.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Beer pong and infinite sirens? Reminds me of my college days. Let's title it: \"Sad-Eyed Sirens of the Lowlands.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yep, always a good call to introduce nukes when you're tired of coming up with good ideas. Let's call it: \"Shelter From the Sirens.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Cliff and Xander spend the rest of their days on Skyros sucking face with sirens and probably let's be honest with each other. Let's call this masterpiece: \"Subterranean Siren Blues.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And then Xander put into effect all the laws he wanted. The first? To finally make crime illegal! Let's title it: \"He Works Hard for the Crypto.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And who delivered the pizza? Why Daphne's missing husband Cliff. This terrible book will be known as: \"Crypto for Nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The moneyed martian Xander will set us up for sequels forever! \"Mo Crypto Mo Problems\" will be a hit!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Amazing! My favorite part was when you dunked on crypto-billionaires. Stupid crypto-billionaires. Let's call it: \"Crypto, Crypto, Crypto in a Rich Man's World.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "All that crazy stuff happened just so we could get back to the procedural we wanted all along. The unflappable Xander will star in our masterpiece: \"Your Blunder Arrest.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Wow ice cream! Then the sirens kill Cliff Fatale I guess. Let's call this mish-mash: \"Sympathy for Doomzilla.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "A daring rescue fit for the gods themselves. Let's call this mystery monster memoir: \"Under My Doomzilla.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Fuzzy handcuffs, huh? You know what? Screw this Xander guy... how come we don't make Doomzilla our protagonist? Now that dude's got rizz. And we would call his story: \"Doomzilla: Rizz Squad.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And the siren does - it was Cliff Fatale! Whom Xander immediately arrests and/or kills. Let's call this: \"Everybody's Got Something to Hide Except Me and My Mermaid.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Huh. Interesting choices... but that's what pushes culture forward, am I right? Anyway, let's call this fartsplosion: \"Xander in the Sea with Mermaids.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Listen I don't wanna backseat drive, but <i>technically</i> there's 50-100 seas. South China, Baltic, Adriatic, etc. Let's call Xander's rise to god of the oceans: \"I Want You (She's a Mermaid).\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_noir_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Haha, you have quite the imagination! A deeply wet and concerning imagination... Anyway! Let's call this: \"Happiness is a Warm Mermaid.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Incredible! Can't wait for the publisher to ruin it with an unnecessary extended universe! Let's title this masterpiece: \"Dolphins Are Snitches: Sirens in Stitches.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Detective stand-up comedy is my favorite thing to laugh at! Same goes for the sirens, who let Cliff go in exchange for a one-hour set from Xander every year. Let's call this: \"The Dolphin Who Saved Cliff Fatale.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's some sort of magic... gun? I'll foreshadow the wizard stuff later, I promise. Let's call this: \"Magic Dolphin Ride.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I wonder if the dolphin watched? The lovemaking, not the rescue. I guess we'll explore that in full detail in... \"She's Always a Siren to Me.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, with the cocaine in there I think our work here is done. Let's call this: \"Xander, the Dolphin and the Yeyo That Brought Them Together.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So I know stories don't need to be \"realistic,\" but I have a hard time buying anyone would ever willingly choose to act in an amateur student film."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_comedy_comedy/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But let's call this: \"Xander's Big Mid-Life Crisis.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And yes of course, Malmoor the Ungodly. Let's put him in the title so that when he comes in at the end nobody returns their book to the store. It'll be called: \"Ride Me Like a Dolphin (Malmoor Is in This).\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Wait is this a story? Or a diary entry? Either way, let's call it: \"Xander's Big Beat Down.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Readers love a good moral. No matter if you're looking for a missing husband, don't jump onto dolphins, people. Let's call this: \"Dial H For Hurricane.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "We could do a tie-in with a famous candy brand! Or a famous dolphin brand... Let's call this: \"I Smell Rain and Candy.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Just goes to show that a good mystery can always be shut down by some bad weather. Anyway, let's call this: \"Cloudy with a Chance of Death.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Definitely - the horny detective saves the day! Or at least, rides off into the sunset on a dolphin. Let's title this incoherent masterpiece: \"A Horny Rain's A-Gonna Fall.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So a happy ending for Xander, and an unhappy one for Cliff (the dolphin kills him). We gotta name this trash so let's call it: \"BDSM: Blowhole, Dorsal, Swimming, Mammal.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "In truth we're all wondering when jorts will make a comeback... but that doesn't necessarily make a good story. Nonetheless, we can title this: \"Squealing Like a Dolphin.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which is where the dolphin came from in the first place! Also Cliff had something to do with the temple too I guess. Maybe he invented temples. Anyway, let's call this: \"A Dolphin's Porpoise.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_comedy_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Same here... but that might just be because I'm here with you, my wonderful writing partner. Honestly though, that's on me, not our potential masterpiece: \"The Blowhole.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, all Daphne asked Xander to do was find her husband, she didn't specify he had to be <i>alive</i>. Let's call this masterpiece: \"Crushed by a Xander.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Seems like there's a lot of loose ends here, not the least of which is 'why is the world's largest jello mold in the middle of the Aegean sea...' Anyway, let's leave it up to the readers to decide the fate of: \"Xander Bounces Back.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And we'll leave it up to the readers to decide what the aliens did to him! Probably something better than we could write in the book titled: \"Abducted: I Guess?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So bad news: the Hague just called — apparently this story containing the words 'fantasized' 'sex' and 'cousin' has been classified as a crime against humanity. But they also suggested a great title: \"Crash and Yearn.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "There's one thing that always quiets a siren - a bullet! This will be called: \"Xander Makes a Mess.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Awesome! And there's definitely a gaping hole in the market for erotic thrillers based on Greek myths, so I think this'll do gangbusters! Let's call it: \"Xander's Sweet Digs.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I mean once we introduce that Daphne is a siren, Xander could definitely be a dragon-born. Let's call this chaotic caper: \"Xander: Call of the Scales.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "At gunpoint, huh? I'll put in a bunch of disclaimers that everyone consented. And had lots of fun. Anyway, let's call this: \"Xander and the Sexy Sirens.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "That'll show Cliff for starting this whole mystery in the first place! This cautionary tale will be titled: \"Don't Mess with Xander Wen.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I mean Cliff and the sirens have to go home somehow, yeah? Yeah... anyway, let's title this: \"Drone of the Dead.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh! And then the spirit/Xander construct booms \"YOU ARE ALL UNDER ARREST, ETERNALLY!\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_adventure_adventure/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What started as a detective story ended as an awesome adventure. And let's title this: \"Ghost in the Military Machine.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ya know, originally I wasn't sure about the tonal shifts, and honestly I'm still not sure. But ending with sex means we'll sell some copies! Let's call this: \"Possessed by Love.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "That's one way to end crime - stop thinking about it! Anyway, let's title this: \"Save a Horse, Ride a Drone.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yeesh, hopefully that's not something you do. Let's title this experimental tome: \"I'm a Slave 4 Drones.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_erotic_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Unfortunately the drone didn't have a setting for \"mythical birthplaces of legendary swords.\" But Xander did end up marrying the drone, so let's call it: \"I Touch My Drone: Excalibur.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_adventure_erotic_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Uh huh, seems like we can cut out the whole beginning part with the mystery and just get to the good stuff. Let's call this: \"Put Your Drone N 2 It.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Bonesaw operator?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_noir/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "You gotta know that's a bad one."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_noir/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Normally I'm generally appreciative, but come the fuck on."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_noir/24
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This story sucks and it's called: \"Naked and Glorious: the Xander Wen Story.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh yeah! Cheesemonger is <i>such</i> a good word! It'll totally make up for the terrible storytelling just for readers to see that lovely word. Let's call this: \"Love, Lust, and Limburger\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And let's be honest, he probably does parkour naked. Anyway, let's call this: \"The Passion and The Parkour.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_noir_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yep, Xander, Cliff, and Daphne all become a throuple. Let's call it: \"The Sirens' Sultry Shores.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_comedy_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Wow. What a profound contemplation on why amateur improv is so useful in society. Let's call it: \"Can I Get a Mystery From the Audience?\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_comedy_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Maybe the readers will pay us to write this one (as it'll release on backwards day). We'll call this strange tale: \"An Improvised Mystery.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_comedy_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So much riches the readers will certainly forget that Xander was ever trying to solve a mystery in the first place! Let's title it: \"There's No Business Like Mystery Business.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_comedy_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, we can't call this one \"Showered in Sexy Underwear\" because that'll ruin the whole story! Oh well, let's call it: \"The Lustful Laughter.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_adventure_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What? Xander knew all along? And then told a dark wizard named Malmoor? Um, let's call this odd tale: \"Xander Drops the Ball.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_adventure_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which of course has magical powers and defeats the wizard! Xander and Cliff (who was kidnapped by the wizard and rescued) smoke a fatty J afterwards. And let's title this paperweight: \"Xander vs. the Forces of Darkness.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_adventure_adventure/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Xander was a dragon-born all along! This will be a real clash of powers. Let's call it: \"Malmoor vs. Xander: Whoever Wins We Lose.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_adventure_erotic/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Sure. This will start as a mystery and end up as a coming-of-age story of a 45 year old detective. Let's call it: \"Awakening Xander's Flower.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_erotic_noir/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Which scared the siren enough to reveal that the siren was Cliff all along! Thrilling. Anyway, let's call this: \"Song of the Siren.\""
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/noir_erotic_erotic_erotic_comedy/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hmm, okay. And then Xander does get overtime. And then he gets gifted Cliff himself for Blissmas. And then the book ends. Great, let's call this: \"Sirens in the Stream.\""
