#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/0 lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/0 lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/0 lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/0 lyric_literature/support_group_horny/0 lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/0 lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/0 lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/0 lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/0
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "This book is..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Splendid!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "We very much enjoyed reading it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/24/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/24/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/24/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/32/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_horny/56/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/24/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/24/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/35/b/1 lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/24/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "Wall! Wall!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "Well developed characterization, excellent prose, all in all a winner."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_good/30
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Perhaps it is not true 'literature', but it should sell quite well in today's marketplace."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...I really wanted to understand it. I just... couldn't!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Don't be so kind. It was an embarrassing mishmash."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "Themes and plot elements were chosen haphazardly - seemingly at random!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/30
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "That's right, Wallace. I felt like I was playing pick-up sticks with all the dropped threads!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/38
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Erotica is easy to do cheaply. It is appreciated that you gave this a modicum of style."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/46
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "An author never reveals their secrets..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_confusing/54
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But we welcome your feedback..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...quite arousing..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "I've read books like this. Under the covers with a flashlight.."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "From ancient Sumerian tablets to Sapphic love poetry, the evolution of erotica continues through you."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/30
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Oh! I didn't know that Wallace. Thanks for the history lesson!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/38
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "I didn't know you had it in you, Lyric. But this... this is a good one."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_sexy/46
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'm full of surprises."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...hysterical!!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "I don't normally laugh."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/24
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "But I <i>almost</i> did."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/35/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "This rivals Aristopanes in tone - a triumph in saturnalian badinage."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/38
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Oh Wallace... I don't know half those words. I'm sure you meant to be nice though!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_comedic/46
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "If you want to make 'em laugh, make 'em laugh."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/16
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "... can I say this out loud?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/24
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "You have my permission."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/32
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "EXTREMELY HORNY."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/40
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Ah. Yes."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/48
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "That."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/59/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "I find myself... stiffened in excitement. I would also recommend that you find some outlet for these... urges of which the characters speak."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/62
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Oh!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/70
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "I liked it. I <i>really</i> liked it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/78/b/1
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Later darling, we'll have a... show and tell."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_horny/81/b/1
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Isn't she excitable."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...awfully exciting!!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "I wasn't on the <i>edge</i> of my seat, but I was closer than I am normally wont to be."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "In the tradition of a true epic - this deserves to be told outside over an open flame."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/30
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "You have a real flair for adventure! I loved it!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_exciting/38
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "This one should fly off the shelves."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...astounding!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "A magnum opus, Lyric. This would stand among the most leather-bound of books."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "I have no words. Save... 'wall'."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/30
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Don't forget me when you're famous."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_fantastic/38
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Thank you, Lyric. For changing my life for the better."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...uh..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/19
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "-trocious."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/27
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "You should be ashamed. We might be your support group, but we are not your punching bags."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/38/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "Some ghastly contrivances like yours can pass themselves off as ironic. Alas, yours stoops lower than even that."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/41
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Oh Wallace... that was cruel."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/49
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Cruel... but accurate."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_terrible/57
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "This 'book' should go no further than we three."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "...oh boy I'm feeling sick..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/16
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "She gets that way when there are too many twists. She prefers being grounded."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/27/b/1
msgctxt "Wallace"
msgid "The torturous plot confounded me. I could not bear another curve, else I might fall."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/30
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "Whoo... I'm going to sit down."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/support_group_twisty/38
msgctxt "Celia"
msgid "Do. And Lyric, perhaps this one should go back to the drawing board."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Thank you for your support!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/8
msgctxt "Florence"
msgid "It's what we do best, Lyric."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/25
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, should we go ahead and publish?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/33/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Absolutely!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/34/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I don't think so..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Marvelous! I'll submit this to Mac right away!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yes... I think you're right. We should go back to the beginning!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/should_we_publish/0/c-1/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The next time you're here let's start again from the top."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/book_review_return/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And once more, we stand to face the music!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/book_review_return/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Let's see what our darling support groupies have to say."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_publish/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Here we go - we're going to find out if our book did well!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_publish/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I can't decide if I feel excited or profoundly ill."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/good_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "They love it! Well, and how could they not."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/good_review/0/11
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'm absolutely over the moon!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/good_review/0/19
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Thank you for your help. I quite literally could not have even started this project without you!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/good_review/0/27/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Anything for you... my love!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/good_review/0/28/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'll always help you, buddy. You're so creative!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well. That could've gone significantly better, I think. Confusing. And embarrassing, even."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "How could you lead me to believe that this was the best work of which I was capable?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "If they knew it was poor, you must've known, and you let me, nay, encouraged me to publish it anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/27
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I may never be able to get published again."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/35/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Yeah. <i>That</i> would be a loss."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/36/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Oh come on. This was all for fun, right?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "No. I mean yes, it was supposed to be fun."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/c-1/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But that wasn't the point. The point was... oh nevermind."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/confusing_review/0/c-1/26
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "You clearly are being deliberately obtuse and I've had more than enough."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/sexy_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well well well! It looks like we've created something wonderfully spicy and arousing!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/sexy_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I wonder... does the co-creation we've birthed indicate any... latent feelings on your part?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/sexy_review/0/16/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "If you're asking if I've got a crush on you... then absolutely I do."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/sexy_review/0/17/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Ha! No no, nothing like that. I did have a blast writing it with you, though!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "We made Celia <i>almost</i> laugh! I don't know if you appreciate how rare that is... but it is the blue diamond of humor."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I could not have even conceived of this project without your help... and I cannot imagine having had any more fun with it than we did!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Thank you. I just wonder... what are we going to get to do now? I'll miss collaborating with you!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Well, we can keep collaborating. Maybe a project a little more... intimate?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "The next time you are ready to write a book, friend, you let me know!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/comedic_review/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "My my. That does sound... fruitful."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well well. We're just arousing everybody today, aren't we?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a delightful tickle!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And what did you think? Did you like it?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Oh I liked it, alright. I <i>really</i> liked it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "You are creative and brave and I think we did a great job!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/horny_review/0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I just wanted to see if you'd write something that stupid. And ya did!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Wow! Did you hear that? They loved it! They were on the edges of their seats!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/11
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, nearly. But to heck with Celia. The others were genuinely enthused!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/19
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah, I am so grateful for your help. Look what we've done! I've gone from embodying literature to creating it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/27
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/35/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "You are so welcome. I really... loved doing this with you. A lot."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/exciting_review/0/36/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "My pleasure! I'm proud of you, friend!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well. I can't really imagine that going any better, can you?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "They were totally blown away! We've got a hit on our hands."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/19
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah, dear you. I truly can't thank you enough for what you've helped me do..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/27
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "...oh goodness, what you've done for me. You've changed me fundamentally and for the better!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/35/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Hey Lyric... I love you. You are worth the help."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/fantastic_review/0/36/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That's what friends do for each other!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Atrocious. They actually used the word atrocious in reference to..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "...to my book. My book. My first book. My big swing to become something I've always wanted to be and never been able to..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And you sabotaged me. You must've seen that it was wretched, just as clearly as the others could see it... and you let me do it anyway."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/24
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And more than that, when I asked you to be honest about whether or not we should publish this drivel, you said yes!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/32
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "How could you. How could you?!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/43/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Just wanted to see if you'd do it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/44/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Because WHO CARES"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/terrible_review/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I cared. You ice-hearted swindler."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well... I think that went pretty well! I think... we made a few of them a little bit motion sick, but there's medication for that."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What do you think? Do you like it?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh hell, how could you not like the book."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/24
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The book isn't really what I'm curious about right now, anyway."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/32
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I've just had the most fun doing this with you. I think I already miss you, miss our collaboration. Tell me... would you come back? Would you come back and see me?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/40
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Maybe to write again of course, but maybe just for me?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/48/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Of course I will. I was mostly here for you anyway!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/twisty_review/0/49/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I think we've got a great friendship going here. And I'll come back to that anytime."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_joiner/12
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "This is so wonderful... with just a bit more of your help, the next book I write will be an epic romance."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_joiner/12
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well! I think I knew I was going to come out of this experience with a book, but to come out of it with a friend as well?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_joiner/20
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What a fabulous bonus!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_joiner/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "It's possible that I don't need to say this; if I were you, I'd have figured it out already."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_joiner/23
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But I'm not you, and thank the written word for that."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_joiner/31
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Get out. Get out and don't come back."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_joiner/61
msgctxt "Reggie"
msgid "Read it and weep."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, hello there! I'm just doing some legwork on my next book."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "My goodness what a fun thing to <i>finally</i> be able to say!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "So I'm just tickled to see you, but I may not be the best conversation partner right now!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/24/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "I'm just saying hi. Book me in for later?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "No need to talk. Keep working! I'll just sit here and read with you."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Actually, I'm ready to Realize you, Lyric."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh look at you with the puns. You're so cute."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Later it is!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, just when I thought this moment couldn't be any more satisfying!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_return/0/c-1/15
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "You and Lyric both immerse yourselves in the written word, silently in love with each other."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hello, friend!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "You just would not believe how productive I have been since I saw you last."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I've got three more books outlined and ready to write!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/24
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And now that I've done all that, I must rest. Absolutely squashed, I'm so tired."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/32/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Better get some rest, then! Glad you're doing well."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/33/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Maybe this'll perk you up... I'm ready to Realize you!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh so am I, I can't even tell you."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_friend_return/0/c-0/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'll chat with you soon when I've got my energy back!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "OH no."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/8/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "That answers that question."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/9/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Listen, Lyric. I... have realized that I was a real jerk before. (USE SMARTS CANDY)"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "No no no. Not you, not me, not here, not ever."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh, figured that out all by yourself, did you?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well. I guess your intelligence was never the problem then, was it?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/23
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I suppose you want to try to be my friend now? Hm."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/31
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I guess if I can be a writer, and I never thought that was possible, I can forgive you after an honest apology."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/39
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Friends it is."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/47
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "For now."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/58/0/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Thanks, Lyric. I do appreciate it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/58/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Hmph."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_hate_return/0/c-1/58/c-0/15
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I'd better get back to writing... that's what I do now and it's very satisfying and it keeps me very, very busy. So. Bye bye."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Truly?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "That's... well, I don't really know <i>what</i> that is, I never thought I'd ever get to contemplate... being real!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Being real. That's always been little more than fiction."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/24
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Unless that's all it is? Fiction?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/32
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Are you spinning a tale for me?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/49/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "No, it's real. And it can happen right now, if you're ready!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/50/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Fiction, for now. But very soon, I'll be able to do it!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_join/0/c-1/10
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Then here I shall remain! Until \"very soon.\" What a delightfully vague phrase that is."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_return/0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, all I'm writing about these days is what it might be like to be human."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_return/0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "The promise you've made me is turning me into a philosopher!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_return/0/25/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Well then, let's get you Realized so you can do your philosophy for real!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_return/0/26/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Keep philosophisin'... I'll be back soon with what I need!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_return/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well, hurry up then! Sometimes I get odd when I think too much."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_begin/6/b/1
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Can we tell a beautiful story with this untested Realization technology?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_begin/9
msgctxt "Skylar"
msgid "Lyric, let's open you to your new Page One!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realize_begin/20
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "The spectral energy flows through your dateviators, and what was once merely all of literature becomes...."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/3
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "Lyric inspects himself, delighting in his transformation. No longer floating before you, he stands on two flesh and blood legs, with a gorgeous head of blonde hair that cascades down his face."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/11
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Well would you take a good, long, appraising look at this specimen before you!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/19
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "I don't know if I'm the most beautiful thing I've ever seen... that honor still goes to the full and verdant potential of my library... but I am not half bad!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/27
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "My goodness, what will I get up to, I wonder?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/35/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Congratulations, friend. I can't wait to see what you do with your new life!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_realized/0/36/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "You know, I've been taking a look at a little book called the Llama Sutra..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/3
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Oh have you now. I know that book very well. It is one of the many that I decided to read more than once."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/11
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Any particular chapters that are sticking out to you?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/19/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Yeah, the one where only one foot is on the ground."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/20/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "There's one that involves honey?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/21/s/0
msgctxt "Choix"
msgid "Ooh! I read something about both of us being upside down."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/c-0/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Yes! And often that's out of 6 or 8 feet total! But we can start moderately."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/c-1/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And in copious amounts, too! I hope there are no bears in your neighborhood."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/c-2/7
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah yes... zero-G lovemaking."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/g-0/0
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Interestingly, the version of the Llama Sutra that I liked the most was actually a workbook. You read it, and then you practiced it."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/g-0/8
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Ah at long last... all this information I hold need not be merely theoretical!"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/g-0/16
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "Come to me, my little love llama."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/g-0/27
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "Let's just say that Lyric had indeed read and practiced <i>everything</i> in the Llama Sutra."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_divert/0/g-0/35
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "It turned out to be one of the most invigorating, exhausting and sexy experiences of your life... Literally."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/0
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "Lyric, in a move that surprised him as much as anyone else, elected not to become a writer."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/8
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He found the concept of sitting on his own while the wide world passed by outside his window to be totally unbearable."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/16
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He discovered that what he wanted more than anything was a deep and rewarding communication with the world around him."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/24
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He wanted a place where he could hear all the languages of the world, all of which, from his extensive reading, he knew fluently. He wanted to hear them spoken, and assist people in understanding each other."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/32
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He became the world's first celebrity translator. He volunteered his services with governments all over the world. He traveled extensively with corporations, humanitarian organizations, even historians and narrative researchers."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/40
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He assisted in documenting, in some cases for the first time in their history, indigenous or remote languages that were threatened with extinction."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/48
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "He works to this day, happy as a clam, surrounded by language. He usually doesn't live in one place for more than a few months at a time, and several people have commented that he must miss having a home of his own."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/56
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "But what they don't understand is that with my languages, I'm home wherever I go. I can always understand the people, and they can understand me..."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/64
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "And where there is good communication, there will be sympathy of spirit."
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/72
msgctxt "Lyric"
msgid "What is home if not that?"
msgstr ""

#: lyric_literature/lyric_love_join/80
msgctxt "Narrator"
msgid "As you can imagine, more than one book has been written <i>about</i> him."
msgstr ""
